<h2 class="doc-h2">Custom Cell Size</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    44px is the smallest touch target most guidance accepts, and a calendar is a grid of
    thirty-one of them.
</p>
<Example Source="CalendarCellSize.razor"><CalendarCellSize /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Week Numbers</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Use <code>ShowWeekNumber</code> to show week numbers. They are ISO 8601, and each one is a
    <code>&lt;th scope="row"&gt;</code>, so a screen reader announces it as the heading of its
    row rather than as another day.
</p>
<Example Source="CalendarWeekNumbers.razor"><CalendarWeekNumbers /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Persian / Hijri / Jalali Calendar</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    A calendar SYSTEM rather than a translation: a Hijri month begins on a different day from the
    Gregorian one and runs 29 or 30 days, and a Persian year starts at the spring equinox. This
    page used to say the section could not exist here because react-day-picker ships the systems —
    .NET ships them too, and the component counts months through whichever one it is given.
</p>
<Example Source="CalendarHijri.razor"><CalendarHijri /></Example>

